Subject: [PATCH] parser: an enum value may begin with true, false or null

The GraphQL specification defines EnumValue as "Name but not `true` or
`false` or `null`" -- the three *names*, not the three prefixes. The
grammar excludes any name that merely starts with one:

    enum_value = ${ !(boolean | null) ~ name }

`!(boolean | null)` is a lookahead for the literal alone, so `boolean`
matches the "true" inside "trueish" and the name is rejected. Anything
called `nullPrefixTestTable_pkey`, `nullable`, `trueish` or `falsey` is
then not lexable as an enum value, and a document naming one is answered
with a parse error.

That is reachable from ordinary schemas. A PostgreSQL constraint called
`nullPrefixTestTable_pkey` is a legal identifier, and an upsert naming it
is a legal request; Hasura's own test corpus has exactly that case
(`graphql_mutation/insert/nullprefixcolumn`).

The fix follows the idiom already used a few lines above for numbers,
which have the same "literal must not run into a name" problem:

    number = @{ (float | int) ~ !name_start }

Reject the literal only where it is *not* followed by a name character,
which is to say only where it is the whole name. `name_continue` is
factored out of `name` so the two cannot drift apart.

Verified against the rule directly, with the three literals and five
names that begin with them:

    true                     rejected    (was rejected)
    false                    rejected    (was rejected)
    null                     rejected    (was rejected)
    nullPrefixTestTable_pkey accepted    (was rejected)
    trueish                  accepted    (was rejected)
    falsey                   accepted    (was rejected)
    nullable                 accepted    (was rejected)
    null_                    accepted    (was rejected)

Unchanged for names that begin with none of them (`ACTIVE`, `_x`, `a1`).

Present in 7.0.17 and unchanged in 7.2.1.

---
--- a/src/graphql.pest
+++ b/src/graphql.pest
@@
-name = @{ name_start ~ (ASCII_ALPHA | ASCII_DIGIT | "_")* }
+name_continue = @{ (ASCII_ALPHA | ASCII_DIGIT | "_") }
+name = @{ name_start ~ name_continue* }
@@
-enum_value = ${ !(boolean | null) ~ name }
+enum_value = ${ !((boolean | null) ~ !name_continue) ~ name }
